abstract: >-
  Open course materials and an example of AI demonstration teaching: the
  course website for the NTNU course Learning Analytics Tools Implementation
  Applications, which teaches students to work with AI coding agents. It
  offers weekly microlearning videos made with AI agents (Codex and Claude)
  and reviewed by the teacher, a browser-based practice computer for
  simulation-based practice, a scenario-based exam, and a student work
  showcase, with the site in four languages. The code is licensed under MIT
  (LICENSE); the course content (videos, posters,
  thumbnails and course text) is licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  (LICENSE-CONTENT.md). Student work and third-party items are not covered
  (NOTICE.md).
